※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ Where a value is wanted of a `match`, every arm ends in a statement that has
※ one and they are all of one type; the block the arms join at carries it out.
※ That is what lets an assignment be pulled out of the arms and written once.

enum Colour { red ; green ; blue }
let chosen: mut Colour = Colour.green
let hundred: mut u8 = 100u8
let seven: mut u8 = 7u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let kept: u8 = match chosen:
        red:
            1u8
        green:
            2u8
        blue:
            3u8
    let more: u8 = match hundred ÷ seven:
        u8(q):
            q
        ⊥:
            0u8
    ※ what this used to say through the exit status, which is six bits now
    if kept + more ≠ 16u8:
        1u6
    else:
        0u6
